# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this a Windows checkout converts to CRLF, and the tests that read a
# file from the repository — the README sample config, the action list, the
# shebang on install.sh — compare against strings written with `\n` and fail
# over a checkout setting rather than over anything they are testing.
#
# install.sh matters beyond the tests: `sh` refuses a script whose shebang line
# ends in CR, so a CRLF copy is not merely untidy but unrunnable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Recordings and stills are binary; normalising them would corrupt them.
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
